WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.300
-Kevin Nealon.
-Wow.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.033
-Looking good, bud.
-That's all I can say is wow.

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:06.033
-Looking good.
We both have beards.

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:07.534
-I have a beard.
I'm growing one for a movie.

00:00:07.534 --> 00:00:08.968
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:10.601
I'm going to see "Top Gun."

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:12.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:13.501
-You're growing it to go see it?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:13.501 --> 00:00:16.200
-Congratulations.
Last time I saw you, by the way,

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.467
I don't know
if you remember this.

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:19.400
We were in Washington, D.C.
-That's right.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.300
-At the Kennedy Center Honors.
-Honoring Lorne Michaels.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.133
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:24.200
-You were so funny that night.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.334
-Thank you.
-Congratulations.

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:26.567
You were really great.

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:29.000
We got to hang out a long time.
-Yeah, we did.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.133
I loved being there
because it was a lot of people.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:33.667
All the "SNL" people.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:36.567
A lot of those people that had
been on "SNL" honoring Lorne.

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:38.033
And we get to hang out
in the green room

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:40.300
with all these people.
-We were doing bits and --

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.701
-Yeah, were punching
everybody's jokes up.

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:43.167
-It was almost
too many bits for me.

00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:45.667
I actually got tired.
-It really was.

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:47.400
-I think it was like five hours
I was there.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.267
And I go,
"I'm ready to take a nap."

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:51.334
-It was a long day.
-Everyone did bits.

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.300
And so it was a long day. I
don't know if you remember this.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.868
I was leaving to go --
They said, "Mr. Fallon,

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:58.200
do you want to go change
in a hotel and put on a tuxedo?"

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.801
I go, "Yeah, I need to get out
of here

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:01.100
because everyone is doing
too many bits."

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.667
-You were exhausted.
-I was tired.

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:04.501
So I'm leaving.
I go to get into my car.

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:07.300
And they go, "Kevin Nealon wants
to say something to you."

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.567
And I go, "Oh, okay.
Where is he?"

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:11.868
They go, "He's in his car."
So I left my car.

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:14.200
I walked across the parking lot.
And you were sitting in the back

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.200
of your limousine with the
window rolled down.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.734
I go, "What's up, Kevin?"

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:20.067
And you looked at me,
and the window rolled up

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:21.200
and you peeled away.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.100
It was the funniest thing --

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.868
It was the funniest thing
at the perfect time.

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:34.200
I was exhausted.
I was like, "What's up, bud?
Anything for you."

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.601
And you just looked at me
and then the window rolled up.

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:38.834
And you took off.
-That was not my fault.

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:41.434
-No?
-My driver was real bossy.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.234
-Oh, yeah, right.
-And he wanted to get home.

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:45.167
And I said, "No, I just called
Jimmy. He's coming over."

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:47.300
He goes, "No, I got to go."
And he starts driving away.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.133
I was furious.
I said, "You got to go back."

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:50.400
He goes, "No, I'm taking you
back to your hotel."

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.534
I lunged over the seat.

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:52.701
I grabbed him by the throat.
-Oh, my God.

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:54.200
I said, "You got to go back."

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.434
-That's a crazy story, Kevin.
I don't believe any of it.

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.868
Grabbed him by the throat.
-I did.

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:01.100
-Let's talk about your book

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.701
"I Exaggerate:
My Brushes with Fame."

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:05.334
It's full of caricatures

00:02:05.334 --> 00:02:07.100
that you've drawn of
different celebrities.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.267
When did this start for you?

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:10.501
-Well, I always loved
drawing caricatures.

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:11.868
I was never that good at it

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:14.033
but I always kind of doodled
as a kid.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.133
I had a painting of
my mother and father

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:19.267
framed as caricatures,
and they were great.

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:20.767
-That you did?
-No, I didn't do it.

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:22.601
Some artist in Paris did it.
And they were great.

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:23.868
They were pastels.

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:25.534
And I lay in bed every night
kind of looking at them.

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:27.133
And I think subconsciously
I was studying them

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:28.934
and how the guy drew them
and everything.

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:32.501
And then, you know, as I got
older, I started doing it more.

00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:34.534
And then when I was on
airplanes, I started sketching

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:35.601
people when they were sleeping.

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:36.701
They're like --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:37.834
And I'd sketch them, you know.

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:39.000
-You would sketch them --
-Yeah.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.200
And I never told them about them
about, though.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.434
Some of those are in the book.
-Like on what?

00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:45.167
-Just on a barf bag or a napkin.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:48.000
It's better to do it with
an empty barf bag.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.734
Because yeah.
-You graduate to --

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:52.868
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-And then, I was in "SNL."

00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:54.167
The table reads, sometimes,

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:56.133
would get a little slow
and monotonous.

00:02:56.133 --> 00:02:57.868
I would start -- if I wasn't
in a sketch, I would start

00:02:57.868 --> 00:02:59.300
sketching the person
across from me,

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.167
whether it's Farley
or Dana Carvey.

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:03.434
You know, and then I'd just --
-We actually have --

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:06.701
this is in the book,
but this is a front page

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:09.701
of a script from "SNL."
-Jeff Daniels.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:10.901
-Jeff Daniels and Farley was

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:11.901
probably sitting
across from you.

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:13.267
-He was sitting across from me.

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:14.834
-This is what you doodled.

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:17.000
-Yeah.
-That is Jeff Daniels.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:19.367
-Amazing.

00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:21.300
And Chris Farley.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.334
-So, that's the kind of stuff
I was doing before I kind of

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:25.200
got into it, really got into it.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.267
-And then how did you go
to the next level?

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:30.167
-Well, a couple years ago,
I used to follow a lot of

00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:34.000
these artists on Instagram,
like Jason Seiler and Paul Moyes

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.200
and some other ones, and
this guy was giving lessons,

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.534
Paul Moyes, over in England.

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:40.934
So they were 500 euros
for 10 lessons.

00:03:40.934 --> 00:03:42.167
I thought, "I like his style.

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:43.567
I'm going to learn how to do it
like he does."

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:46.634
And so I took lessons from him
on Skype.

00:03:46.634 --> 00:03:47.901
-That's how you learned how to
do it?

00:03:47.901 --> 00:03:49.367
I mean, this is the photo.

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:52.200
This is the painting
that you did of Farley.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.701
[ Audience aws ]
-Yeah.

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:55.834
-I mean, that's amazing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:58.868
It almost comes right at you.

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:00.634
-I mean, that was
such a common look.

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:04.367
And on each -- So, each picture
on the opposite page has

00:04:04.367 --> 00:04:05.968
a little anecdote
about that person

00:04:05.968 --> 00:04:08.467
and the experience
I had with them.

00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:12.100
By the way, all of these
are on kevinnealonart.com.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.467
That's where you can find these
paintings and also my book.

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:16.467
-Yeah. Kevinnealonart.com.

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:20.200
I also saw one of my favorites.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.033
Dana Carvey. You did Dana.
-Dana Carvey, yeah.

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:23.367
-That's Dana Carvey there
you did.

00:04:23.367 --> 00:04:26.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:29.801
I noticed I wasn't in the book.

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:31.167
You know, it doesn't matter.

00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:33.133
-Well, you should thank me
for that.

00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:34.868
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:37.934
-Here's the problem, Jimmy.
This has ruined my life.

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:40.801
Because as a caricature artist,
you look around.

00:04:40.801 --> 00:04:42.434
Everyone you look at, you see

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:43.734
their features
that are outstanding.

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:46.434
So it's like walking through
a fun house every day.

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:49.033
And everybody looks kind of like
distorted and stuff.

00:04:49.033 --> 00:04:51.467
And it's a little freaky.
-What about them sticks out?

00:04:51.467 --> 00:04:55.334
A big nose or --
-Yeah, but now you -- you have,

00:04:55.334 --> 00:04:57.667
like, -- you know, in fact,
I actually did one of you.

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:58.934
Let me get it out for you.

00:04:58.934 --> 00:05:00.601
[ Cheers ]

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.834
Now, this one I really
enjoyed doing.

00:05:03.834 --> 00:05:06.133
You don't really have a lot of
outstanding characteristics.

00:05:06.133 --> 00:05:07.467
Well, do you want to hold it?
-Thank you.

00:05:07.467 --> 00:05:09.534
-Do you want me to unveil it?
-I can do it, yeah.

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:11.000
Let me hold it.
Alright, this is it.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.434
-Ready? I'm going to unveil it.
Ready?

00:05:12.434 --> 00:05:14.133
One, two, three.

00:05:14.133 --> 00:05:17.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:19.567
-Are you kidding me?

00:05:19.567 --> 00:05:21.868
Kevin!

00:05:21.868 --> 00:05:23.200
I love it.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:25.234
Kevin, I'm like -- this is --
I'm honored.

00:05:25.234 --> 00:05:26.834
-Oh, I got to sign it.
I forgot to sign it.

00:05:26.834 --> 00:05:28.901
-Yeah, could you?
-Yeah. Yeah, sure.

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:30.601
-Kevin, this is amazing.
-Oh, my pleasure, man.

00:05:30.601 --> 00:05:32.501
My pleasure.
-You were one of my --

00:05:32.501 --> 00:05:35.467
-Well, you know, it's not easy.
It's not easy, Jimmy.

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:36.934
-Thank you.
-No.

00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:38.834
And, you know, sometimes
it takes me a long time.

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:40.300
I go through a little process.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.467
You know, where I have to --
I'm not quite getting it right.

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:44.501
Do another one, another one,
another one. It's an evolution.

00:05:44.501 --> 00:05:46.667
-We have a video that shows how
your portraits come together.

00:05:46.667 --> 00:05:49.300
-Alright. This is you, I think.
Yeah.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:52.334
Start like that.
-Wow.

00:05:52.334 --> 00:05:54.367
-It takes a while.

00:05:54.367 --> 00:05:55.834
-Wow!

00:05:55.834 --> 00:05:57.467
-Spent a long time on you,
Jimmy.

00:05:57.467 --> 00:05:59.767
-You're really -- Kevin, wow!

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:00.934
That's amazing.

00:06:00.934 --> 00:06:03.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:03.667 --> 00:06:06.167
-But here's the thing.

00:06:06.167 --> 00:06:09.267
I didn't know he grew a beard
since I did this one.

00:06:09.267 --> 00:06:11.801
I didn't know. And so, a couple
days, they told me.

00:06:11.801 --> 00:06:13.667
So I had to add on to it.

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:15.033
And I didn't know how long
you're going to have that beard,

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:18.767
so I took some creative measures
here, and this is kind of

00:06:18.767 --> 00:06:20.167
how I went about doing that.

00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:23.601
-Me with a beard.

00:06:23.601 --> 00:06:26.067
Yes. This is great.

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:28.601
Kevin.
-Yeah, I didn't know how long.

00:06:28.601 --> 00:06:38.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.634
I didn't know how long
you were gonna have the beard.

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:42.834
-I got to say
I'm honored that you did this.

00:06:42.834 --> 00:06:44.267
You're one of my favorite
comedians.

00:06:44.267 --> 00:06:46.334
I've always looked up to you
and loved you.

00:06:46.334 --> 00:06:48.067
And you've always been great
to me. This means a lot to me.

00:06:48.067 --> 00:06:49.267
-Thank you, buddy.
-Thank you so much for this.

00:06:49.267 --> 00:06:50.734
-It's $50.

00:06:50.734 --> 00:06:53.133
-Also, by the way, if you want
to see something funny,

00:06:53.133 --> 00:06:54.734
"Hiking with Kevin" returns for

00:06:54.734 --> 00:06:55.734
its fourth season
on October 27th.

00:06:55.734 --> 00:06:57.033
-That's right. October 27th.

00:06:57.033 --> 00:06:59.300
-Oh, my gosh.
By the way, you film it.

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.234
You edit it. You do everything.
-I do it all, man.

00:07:01.234 --> 00:07:03.667
I've done 100 hikes already.
I'm exhausted.

00:07:03.667 --> 00:07:06.767
-But it's so good, but you
never -- you never let anyone

00:07:06.767 --> 00:07:07.901
know who you're hiking with.

00:07:07.901 --> 00:07:10.300
-No, it's always a surprise.
-But why?

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:12.701
-Because I like people to tune
in to see who it is.

00:07:12.701 --> 00:07:14.667
-Yeah, but if you tell me who it
is, I would tune in.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:16.133
-Well, I'm going to tell you who
it is this season.

00:07:16.133 --> 00:07:17.367
I'll tell you a couple of them.

00:07:17.367 --> 00:07:19.734
By the way, I started about four
or five years ago,

00:07:19.734 --> 00:07:22.033
and the hikes were
very difficult, you know.

00:07:22.033 --> 00:07:24.767
And each year it's getting
a little less, a little less,

00:07:24.767 --> 00:07:27.200
and a little less,
and now it's flat.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:28.734
-Walking to Starbucks
with Kevin.

00:07:28.734 --> 00:07:30.601
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.601 --> 00:07:34.000
-But what I do, Jimmy, is if
it's flat, I'll hold the camera

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.968
on an angle so it looks
like we're going up a hill.

00:07:35.968 --> 00:07:39.501
-So smart. Come on, buddy.
Come on.

00:07:39.501 --> 00:07:41.133
I want to show everyone
a preview of

00:07:41.133 --> 00:07:42.667
season four of
"Hiking with Kevin."

00:07:42.667 --> 00:07:44.033
Take a look at this.

00:07:44.033 --> 00:07:47.400
-You love the container store.
Am I right?

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.801
-I do. Yes.

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:51.667
The first time I went into a
container store, I lost my mind.

00:07:51.667 --> 00:07:53.200
-Me too.
Let me ask you this.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.200
-Yes?
-Who's your favorite Beatle?

00:07:57.033 --> 00:07:59.133
-Your questions are terrible.

00:07:59.133 --> 00:08:01.667
But -- No, I mean,
in a good way.

00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:08.501
-♪ I'll be so blue
just thinking about you ♪

00:08:08.501 --> 00:08:10.000
-You're good.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.501
-When was the last time
you washed your car?

00:08:13.501 --> 00:08:16.701
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:16.701 --> 00:08:18.868
-This has just been
the most brutal

00:08:18.868 --> 00:08:21.400
hour and a half of my life.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.868
-Hey, Eugene.
-Kevin.

00:08:23.868 --> 00:08:25.400
-Hey, buddy,
thanks for doing the hike.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.234
-I didn't know it was today.

00:08:27.234 --> 00:08:30.734
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:08:30.734 --> 00:08:32.734
-Kevin Nealon, everybody.

00:08:32.734 --> 00:08:35.167
"Hiking with Kevin"
premieres October 27th.

00:08:35.167 --> 00:08:39.133
His book "I Exaggerate:
My Brushes with Fame"

00:08:39.133 --> 00:08:41.501
is available for pre-order
right now.

00:08:41.501 --> 00:08:43.200
It's funny. It's awesome.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.567
We'll be right back with
stand-up from Sabrina Wu.

00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:46.801
Stick around, everybody.

